/P 90 0 R
/E (Expected Shortfall \(ES\) is superior for capturing tail risk, but its estimation at extreme quantiles remains challenging. Traditional scaling methods are unreliable due to non-normality and autocorrelation. Enhanced scaling techniques such as the Cornish-Fisher expansion and autocorrelation analysis can substantially improve VaR assessment accuracy in financial contexts.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [0 1]
